    "updated_at": "2015-10-30T02:22:30Z",
    "body": "Apologies if I'm confusing things by force pushing squashed commits. This is my first time sending a pull request to HTML and I'm not yet sure of the best way to do things.\n\nAnyway, I've updated my branch to address:\n- the missing [NewObject]\n- explicitly mentioning copying, as Anne requested\n\nI've stuck to DOMMatrix rather than DOMMatrixInit, because I think it's better to be consistent with the existing methods. I could be wrong, but I don't expect many people will call setTransform with a long list of matrix values. Rather they'll use it to either reset the transform to a known state (i.e. a transform-only version of save/restore) or set it to a value copied from elsewhere (e.g. the getTransform() of another canvas).\n",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
